        "original_id": "6e0417c0-6c8b-5d26-8b22-95de8d8b5560",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: English National Ballet, English National Opera, BBC Television\n- Places: London Coliseum, Royal Albert Hall, St. Martin's Lane, central London\n- People: Alina Cojocaru, Frank Matcham, Oswald Stoll\n- Roles: principal dancer, theatrical architect, impresario\n- Events: performances, opening, first performance\n- Works: Doctor Ox's Experiment\n\nFacts:\n- The London Coliseum opened on 24 December 1904 as the London Coliseum Theatre of Varieties on St. Martin's Lane in central London.\n- Frank Matcham designed the London Coliseum for the impresario Oswald Stoll.\n- The London Coliseum was built as one of London's largest and most luxurious family variety theatres.\n- Doctor Ox's Experiment was first performed on 15 June 1998 at the London Coliseum by English National Opera.\n- English National Opera co-commissioned Doctor Ox's Experiment with BBC Television.\n- As of November 2013, Alina Cojocaru was a principal dancer with the English National Ballet.\n- The English National Ballet regularly performs seasons at the London Coliseum.\n- The English National Ballet has been noted for specially staged performances at the Royal Albert Hall.",
